course: dictionary
lesson: 4008
title: Garden: one word, many places
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: A garden is a piece of land where people grow flowers, fruit or vegetables. In «Climbing fences can break things in the garden and you can get hurt.», the word garden is a place outside, with plants and fences around it.
explain: In the UK, Ireland, Australia and New Zealand, the garden is also the grass area around a house. Americans often call this place the yard. Look at the words near garden to see which meaning fits, such as «back garden» or «gardening gloves».
explain: Garden can also be a verb. To garden is to work in a garden, planting, weeding and watering. A garden can also be a public park with plants, like botanical gardens.
fact: Garden (noun) means a piece of land where people grow flowers, fruit or vegetables.
fact: Garden (verb) means to work in a garden: planting, weeding and watering.
fact: «Vegetable garden», «flower garden» and «back garden» tell you what the garden is for or where it is.
fact: «That cheerful robin is also one of the fiercest birds in the garden.» Robins fight other robins to keep their patch.
fact: Plants need sun, water and soil to grow, so a school garden shows how seeds grow.
exercise: What is a garden? | A tall building with many floors | *A piece of land where people grow flowers, fruit or vegetables | A shop that sells bread | A room inside a house for cooking
exercise: In Australia the garden is the grass area around a house. What do Americans often call this place? | Street | Kitchen | *Yard | Castle
exercise: Dad says, «I spent all morning gardening.» What is he doing? | Sleeping late | Cooking dinner | Swimming in a lake | *Working in the garden, planting, weeding and watering
test: In «That cheerful robin is also one of the fiercest birds in the garden», what kind of place is the garden? | A pond | Inside a kitchen | *Outdoors, where plants and birds live | A car park
test: Which phrase means a garden for growing food? | Botanical garden | *Vegetable garden | Back garden | Flower garden
exam: «Its red breast is a warning flag, and it will fight other robins to keep its patch.» What does the robin do to protect its patch? | *Fights other robins to keep it | Gives its food away to the other robins | Hides under the car | Flies off to the kitchen
